\details{
Returns canonical long output by default, or list-column or both
representations when requested. Per-pair isochrone failures returned by a
provider are preserved as NA-propagated rows with
\code{failure_origin = "isochrone"}. Batch-level provider errors still abort so
callers do not mistake a failed run for a complete analytic result.

The orchestrator selects one of four execution paths based on which bypass
arguments (\code{precomputed_isochrones}, \code{acs}) are supplied:
\itemize{
\item Both \code{NULL} (default): runs the full
\code{\link[=cacs_acs_prefetch]{cacs_acs_prefetch()}} -> \code{\link[=cacs_isochrone]{cacs_isochrone()}} ->
\code{\link[=cacs_intersect_weight]{cacs_intersect_weight()}} -> \code{\link[=cacs_propagate_moe]{cacs_propagate_moe()}} ->
\code{\link[=cacs_derive_rates]{cacs_derive_rates()}} chain.
\item \code{precomputed_isochrones} supplied: skips \code{\link[=cacs_isochrone]{cacs_isochrone()}}.
\item \code{acs} supplied: skips \code{\link[=cacs_acs_prefetch]{cacs_acs_prefetch()}}.
\item Both supplied: skips both fetch steps (the fully offline,
no-network mode used by the example below).
}
